# The Engine page's scope: the voice's wave, locked to the pitch the voice plays, so a held note's trace
# holds still; quiet, a flat line. Two periods across: the trace's halves match (to a px on average), it
# doesn't move from one trace to the next, nor in 5 s; it doesn't redraw while it holds; and its size
# doesn't follow MASTER.
wait 200
tap HOME
expect view 1
# quiet: nothing locked, nothing stale
expect scope_period 0
expect scope_trail 0
expect stale 0
shot scope_quiet.png
# A4 (69): 44117.647 / 440 = 100.27 samples (the periods: as the voice plays them, Plaits' tables)
midi 90 45 64
breath 0 100 50
wait 300
expect level >5
expect scope_period 1003
expect scope_note 69
expect scope_trail >0
expect scope_cycle <10
expect scope_still <10
# Classic: Morph's live value on the right
expect scope_label Morph_25
expect stale 0
shot scope_light.png
# held, it holds: 2 s with no more than a few redraws (a redraw each read, every other frame: 60)
expect blits >-1
wait 2000
expect blits <12
# ...and still there 5 s on: it locks to the pitch the voice plays (Plaits' tables, to 1/256 semitone),
# not the exact note's, which drifts by a period every ten seconds or so
scopemark
wait 5000
expect scope_since <10
# a low note: E2 (40), 535.5 samples (the ring's points are means of 4)
midi 80 45 0
midi 90 28 64
wait 300
expect scope_period 5355
expect scope_cycle <10
expect scope_still <10
# a high one: C7 (96), 21.08 samples
midi 80 28 0
midi 90 60 64
wait 300
expect scope_period 211
expect scope_cycle <10
expect scope_still <10
scopemark
wait 5000
expect scope_since <10
# legato from C7 down to E1 (28), 1071 samples: C7's trace stays, under C7's name, until there are two
# periods of E1 to show (no C7 under E1's name), and then it goes (none left in the trail)
midi 90 1C 64
midi 80 60 0
wait 10
expect scope_note 96
expect scope_cycle <10
wait 10
expect scope_note 96
expect scope_cycle <10
wait 10
expect scope_note 96
expect scope_cycle <10
wait 10
expect scope_note 96
expect scope_cycle <10
wait 10
expect scope_note 96
expect scope_cycle <10
wait 20
expect scope_note 28
expect scope_trail 1
expect scope_period 10710
expect scope_cycle <10
# up and down an octave on the same ring points (d 1), A4 to A5 and back every 33 ms, so some change
# lands just before a read: each read only from the note it names
midi 90 45 64
midi 80 1C 0
wait 300
midi 90 51 64
midi 80 45 0
wait 33
expect scope_cycle <10
midi 90 45 64
midi 80 51 0
wait 33
